From 4759e3b2b04a4ceeeb18e26517ddb85a248cb1bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:30:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(pwa): restore installable PWA with an offline-capable
 app shell

The 0.8.16 line shipped only a manifest and a notification-only worker, so
the app had no cache layer at all: every launch refetched the whole bundle,
and `notification-sw.js` competed for the `/` scope with any app worker,
which would silently replace it.

- sw.js: navigation is network-first (falls back to the cached shell, then
  offline.html), hashed build assets are cache-first, brand files are
  cache-first with background revalidation. API / Socket.IO / health /
  upload stay untouched. The worker installs without skipWaiting so a new
  build never swaps hashed chunks under a running page; it activates on the
  next cold start, and `SKIP_WAITING` is still honoured on request.
- offline.html: self-contained, theme-aware fallback.
- Icon set: 192/512 any plus a 512 maskable that keeps the artwork inside
  the 80% safe circle, and a dedicated apple-touch-icon.
- manifest: adds id/display_override/orientation/launch_handler and points
  at the real icon sizes instead of one 1254px logo.
- usePwa: single page-wide registration (the old one re-registered on every
  call and leaked listeners and timers), secure-context guard, update
  detection, and shell-cache warmup.
- completion-notification: reuse the app worker, drop notification-sw.js.
- static-cache: never cache sw.js or the manifest (that would pin clients
  to a stale shell) and give brand files a real max-age, since without it
  `serve` emits max-age=0 and every launch on a plain-HTTP origin
  re-downloads the 1 MB logo.

Verified on HTTPS: assets transfer 0 KB on the 2nd/3rd load and the app
still renders offline. On plain HTTP the worker cannot register (not a
secure context), but repeat loads now also transfer 0 KB.
